# Linux (LF) newlines, in every file, on every machine.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config. That leaves
# the committed blobs LF but hands the WORKING COPY CRLF, so a checkout here
# reads byte-different from the same commit on Linux or macOS while
# `git status` still reports clean. That is exactly how a comparison of this
# folder against its GitHub copy came back showing every line of every file
# changed when the content was in fact identical.
#
# Declared here, the rule travels with the repository and no longer depends on
# how a given machine happens to be configured.
#
# Every tracked file is text (*.py, *.md, LICENSE, .gitignore) and every blob
# is ALREADY stored LF, verified byte-exactly: `git add --renormalize .` under
# this rule produces no index change, so nothing below rewrites history.

* text=auto eol=lf
